WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.667 --> 00:00:17.427
Danny: I hope it's clay today.

2
00:00:17.428 --> 00:00:20.340
Brad: You always hope it’s clay.

3
00:00:20.341 --> 00:00:23.475
Danny: Modeling clay is the best!

4
00:00:23.476 --> 00:00:27.910
Tina: I wish it were gym class.

5
00:00:27.911 --> 00:00:32.612
Mr. Smith: Children, please. Please sit down.

6
00:00:32.613 --> 00:00:34.665
Danny: I hope it’s clay.

7
00:00:34.666 --> 00:00:38.261
Please, I hope it’s clay.

8
00:00:38.262 --> 00:00:41.518
Mr. Smith: Today, for art class we will be using . . .

9
00:00:41.519 --> 00:00:47.277
Danny: CLAY?

10
00:00:47.278 --> 00:00:50.144
Mr. Smith: Yes, Danny, we’re using clay.

11
00:00:50.145 --> 00:00:52.231
Not so loud next time.

12
00:00:52.232 --> 00:00:55.074
Danny: Sorry.

13
00:00:55.075 --> 00:00:57.574
Brad: You’re always so excited!

14
00:00:57.575 --> 00:01:04.018
Danny: Shh. I don’t want to get into more trouble!

15
00:01:04.019 --> 00:01:06.112
Mr. Smith: Here you go, Tina.

16
00:01:06.113 --> 00:01:09.545
Tina: I just want black and white please.

17
00:01:09.546 --> 00:01:11.629
Mr. Smith: Why is that, Tina?

18
00:01:11.630 --> 00:01:18.566
Tina: Well, those are the colors of a soccer ball.

19
00:01:18.567 --> 00:01:22.769
Brad: Actually, black isn’t really a color.

20
00:01:22.770 --> 00:01:24.361
Mr. Smith: Very good, Brad.

21
00:01:24.362 --> 00:01:28.247
Black is really no color at all.

22
00:01:28.248 --> 00:01:30.310
Danny: How did you know that?

23
00:01:30.311 --> 00:01:34.778
Brad: My computer has all the answers.

24
00:01:34.779 --> 00:01:41.779
Mr. Smith: Children, I’m handing out seven colors because . . .

25
00:01:41.780 --> 00:01:44.381
Danny: Who’s this guy Roy?

26
00:01:44.382 --> 00:01:47.066
Mr. Smith: Well, if you’d let me explain . . .

27
00:01:47.067 --> 00:01:52.464
Danny: Is he a new kid in class?

28
00:01:52.465 --> 00:01:58.020
Mr. Smith: No, Danny, Roy G. Biv is . . .

29
00:01:58.021 --> 00:02:01.936
A cloud. It must have been a cloud.

30
00:02:01.937 --> 00:02:05.588
Danny: Who is Roy G. Biv?

31
00:02:05.589 --> 00:02:08.235
Mr. Smith: Yes. That’s what I was saying.

32
00:02:08.236 --> 00:02:10.639
Roy G. Biv stands for . . .

33
00:02:10.640 --> 00:02:15.332
Tina: Red, orange, yellow, green, blue . . .

34
00:02:15.333 --> 00:02:17.227
Brad: I knew that.

35
00:02:17.228 --> 00:02:20.131
Mr. Smith: Very good, Tina. Keep going.

36
00:02:20.132 --> 00:02:24.845
Tina: Well, those are the colors in front of me.

37
00:02:24.846 --> 00:02:27.104
Mr. Smith: Brad, do you know the rest?

38
00:02:27.105 --> 00:02:28.998
Brad: Indigo and violet.

39
00:02:28.999 --> 00:02:31.948
The colors of the rainbow.

40
00:02:31.949 --> 00:02:35.229
Mr. Smith: Very good, Brad!

41
00:02:35.230 --> 00:02:37.089
Danny: Can we start?

42
00:02:37.090 --> 00:02:41.353
My imagination is going crazy!!

43
00:02:41.354 --> 00:02:44.013
Mr. Smith: Danny, it’s not nice to interrupt.

44
00:02:44.014 --> 00:02:46.228
Mr. Smith: Class, you may now begin.

45
00:02:46.229 --> 00:02:52.120
Create whatever you want.

46
00:02:52.121 --> 00:02:53.924
Tina: What are you doing?

47
00:02:53.925 --> 00:02:55.822
Danny: I’m just looking.

48
00:02:55.823 --> 00:02:57.139
Tina: At what?

49
00:02:57.140 --> 00:03:00.493
Danny: What are you making?

50
00:03:00.494 --> 00:03:02.325
Is it a tree?

51
00:03:02.326 --> 00:03:06.729
Tina: It’s going to be a soccer player.

52
00:03:06.730 --> 00:03:11.769
Danny: That gives me an idea!

53
00:03:11.770 --> 00:03:15.069
Brad: How’s it going over there, Mr. Artist?

54
00:03:15.070 --> 00:03:18.079
Danny: I don’t think I’ve got it right yet.

55
00:03:18.080 --> 00:03:21.123
Mr. Smith: Danny, more art and less talk.

56
00:03:21.124 --> 00:03:30.133
Danny: But when I talk, it helps my hands move!
